```js
const search = instantsearch({
  indexName: "products",
  searchClient,
  initialUiState: {
    products: {
      query: "fakequerythatshouldreturnnoresults",
      refinementList: {
        Designer: ["Zimmermann"]
      }
    }
  }
});

const virtualRefinementList = instantsearch.connectors.connectRefinementList(
  () => null
);
const virtualSearchBox = instantsearch.connectors.connectSearchBox(
  () => null
);

search.addWidgets([
  virtualSearchBox(),
  virtualRefinementList({ attribute: "Designer" }),
  instantsearch.widgets.hits({
    container: "#hits",
    templates: {
      item: `<div>{{Designer}} - {{ProductTitle}}</div>`
    }
  })
]);
```

This is what's meant with "virtual widget".

Thanks for pointing out that [this section](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/upgrade-guides/js/#searchparameters) is indeed insufficient to follow if  you didn't already  use advanced InstantSearch features.

Another option is the following:

```js
search.addWidgets([
  instantsearch.widgets.configure(
      { disjunctiveFacetsRefinements: {"Designer":["Zimmermann"]} }
  ),
]);
```
